{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "גם עלה", :translit "gam alah", :gloss "also go up"} {:he "בה\"א", :translit "ba-heh", :gloss "with a heh"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Letter heh on עלה hints at five generations: Jacob, Levi, Kehat, Amram, Moses"}], :frame {:text "The verse records God's assurance to Jacob: 'I myself will go down with you to Egypt, and I myself will also bring you up' (Genesis 46:4). The lineage from Jacob through Moses runs exactly five generations.", :sources ["Genesis 46:4"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ויוסף ישית ידו על עיניך", :translit "veyosef yashit yado al einekha", :gloss "and Joseph shall place his hand upon your eyes"} {:he "יעצים עיניך", :translit "ya'atzim einekha", :gloss "shall close your eyes"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Placing hand on eyes means closing eyes at death"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'and Joseph shall place his hand upon your eyes' is understood as the idiom for a son closing a parent's eyes at death. Earlier God promised Jacob 'do not fear going down to Egypt' (Genesis 46:3); here he is assured Joseph will be present at his death.", :sources ["Genesis 46:3" "Genesis 46:4"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Letter heh on עלה hints at five generations: Jacob, Levi, Kehat, Amram, Moses", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Placing hand on eyes means closing eyes at death", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:11:45.402726505Z", :model "glm-5.2"}